# 2026-09-02 (9) -- 47/39 -> 48/40: the E2-b3 M1 carrier --
# `method_overload_pick` (two `absorb` overloads split by the argument's
# type): the method key is TYPED (the same `typed_call_key` door the generic
# path used), the walk types arguments BEFORE the judge (the free-call order
# of 2026-08-21 arriving at method calls), and the pick decides the SYMBOL --
# each call names its own overload's C spelling. A real D84 tie (modes varying
# oppositely) refuses by name; the oracle agrees on this axis
# (E_OVERLOAD_AMBIGUOUS_MODE). Reverse probe: the key door degraded to the
# arity key -- both M1 holders redden.
# 2026-09-02 (10) -- 48/40 -> 49/41: the char-literal wave carrier --
# `char_literal` (a codepoint and an escape between single quotes, compared
# on an own fn's param): the lexer gains the quote branch (verbatim text,
# escapes consume two bytes, the empty pair and an unclosed run stay
# ErrorTok), the checker judges WIDTH/escape/unicode by name, `char` joins
# Prims (universe ordinal 14) and `is_primitive` (equality admits it), and
# the codepoint is spelled by the ONE mangle door (`'x'` -> 120). println of
# a char stays refused: the oracle prints a literal as the glyph and a bound
# value as its code -- the asymmetry is filed for the registry, not copied.
# Reverse probe: the lexer branch behind `false &&` -- four holder failures.
# 2026-09-02 (11) -- 49/41 -> 50/42: the coalesce wave carrier -- `coalesce`
# (`xs.get(i) ?? 0`, both branches): `??` is one lexeme (a lone `?` stays an
# ErrorTok -- Try is not a subset form), a POSTFIX link of the chain whose
# right side is a primary (the oracle's `parse_unary` shape), a Coalesce node
# typed by the LEFT side's payload (never the right's -- the oracle's own
# rule), and an emission that hoists a temporary and fills it under a tag
# guard, with the fallback emitted INSIDE the else branch: that placement IS
# the short circuit. `?? return` is retracted (D86 amend) -- parsed, refused
# by name. Reverse probe: the parser link behind `false &&` -- three holder
# failures and the carrier smoke red. Self-read: syntax 322 -> 272.
# 50/42 -> 51/43 (2026-09-03, 274.6 V2b): carrier examples/basics/named_tuple.nv
# -- the parenthesised record form constructed BY CALL, with defaults and a
# named argument (`Pair(1, 2)`, `Complex()`, `Complex(re: 3.5)`). The
# constructor is registered as an ordinary function row (the owner's rule), so
# arity, named arguments and defaults are the existing resolver's answers and
